// Package adt is the abstract syntax of the Tom compiler (the engine
// ADT), generated by gomgo (tom/gom/backend) from the .gom files of this
// directory: the Go compiler's own copies of the Java compiler's
// src/tom/engine/adt/*.gom, with the same sorts, operators and slots
// (checked by TestSignatureParity, tom/internal/adtgen) and hooks
// written in Tom+Go, so that the Go ASTs can evolve independently of the
// Java ones. As in build.xml, Il.gom is generated alone, into package
// tom/engine/adt/il; this package holds the other 14 modules (the import
// closure of TomSignature.gom).
//
// The package is generated as any Gom module (gomgo gom-batch, see
// tom/internal/adtgen): one <module>.go per .gom file with the Java Gom
// API and lists as maximally-shared cons cells, and the Tom mapping
// adt.tom, which a Tom+Go program includes to match and build these
// terms. The hooks:
//
//   - the AU theories of AndConstraint, OrConstraint (with the neutral
//     elements TrueConstraint() and FalseConstraint()) and
//     OrConstraintDisjunction are generated in Go (Cons<Op>);
//   - the rules of Code.gom and TomExpression.gom, the make hooks of
//     Cast and NameNumber and the make_insert hooks of concInstruction
//     and concTomNumber are Tom+Go code of the mapping; hooks.t, which
//     includes the mapping, is compiled by tom -go into hooks.go, whose
//     init functions install them (Hook<Make> variables).
//
// hooks_test.go pins their observable effects.
//
// # Regeneration
//
// From the repository root (needs a built Tom distribution, src/dist,
// or TOM_HOME, for hooks.go):
//
//	mage -d magefiles -w . regenAdt
//
// TestSelfBootstrap (tom/internal/adtgen) checks that the committed
// sources are byte-identical to a fresh regeneration; they are never
// edited by hand.
package adt
